<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9071" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">collĭgātĭo</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">conl-</span></b> ),
			ōnis, f.
		2. colligo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a binding together</i>, <i>connection</i> (rare). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Prop.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ex his colligationibus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Univ. 7, 21</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tota operis colligatio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Val.
					Max. 8, 14, 6</span></i>
			; cf.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">inter quattuor (elementa),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Macr. Somn. Scip. 1, 6, 28</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b> In
			mechanics, <i>a ligature</i>, <i>band</i>, <i>fastening</i>, <i><span class="en">Vitr. 10,
			1</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b> (only in Cic.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">causarum omnium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Div. 1, 56, 127</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">colligatione naturali omnia fiunt,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Fat. 14, 31</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">artior societatis propinquorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Off. 1, 17, 53</span></i>
			.</div>
